    "description": "**About Cyagen Biosciences**\n\nCyagen Biosciences is a global leader in AI-driven, fully human antibody drug R&D and preclinical CRO services. Founded in 2006 as a High-Tech Enterprise, Cyagen leverages proprietary gene-editing technology and integrated platforms \u2014 including HUGO-Ab, AbSeek, and HUGO-GT \u2014 to enable target validation, antibody discovery, screening, and functional validation across oncology, autoimmune, metabolic, and other key disease areas.\n\n**Role Overview**\n\nOur scientific support team is expanding, and we're looking for talented scientists who combine deep technical expertise with strong communication skills to help researchers accelerate drug discovery and development.\n\n**Key Responsibilities**\n\nCustomer-Facing Scientific Support\n\n* Serve as the technical bridge between customers and internal R&D/production teams, ensuring accurate and efficient communication throughout project delivery.\n\nBusiness Development Enablement\n\n* Support the BD team with technical consultations for animal models, CRO services, and related solutions.\n\nCross-Functional Collaboration\n\n* Work closely with internal R&D, production, and commercial teams to translate customer requirements into deliverable scientific solutions.\n\nScientific & Market Development\n\n* Stay current with advances in molecular biology, immunology, oncology, neuroscience, antibody engineering, and pharmacology; share insights with the team.\n* Provide field feedback to help optimize Cyagen's platforms and services.\n\nExternal Engagements\n\n* Deliver compelling technical presentations and training to customers and internal colleagues.\n* Travel to meet customers, attend conferences, and support commercial activities and industry events.\n\n**What We're Looking For**\n\nEssential\n\nPhD in Molecular Biology, Antibody Engineering, Immunology, Oncology, Neuroscience, Pharmacology, or a related life-science field (required).\n\nExperience working within a biotechnology, pharmaceutical, CRO, life-science tools, or related organization (required \u2013 3 years minimum).\n\nStrong scientific understanding of biological research and experimental methodologies.\n\n* Knowledge of animal models, gene editing, antibody discovery, preclinical pharmacology, or CRO services.\n* Ability to understand complex scientific problems and translate them into practical experimental or service solutions.\n* Excellent communication, interpersonal, and presentation skills:\n* Able to convey scientific concepts to researchers and other technical audiences. Confident engaging with business stakeholders.\n* Excellent verbal and written communication skills in English.\n* Strong organization, prioritization, and time management skills, with resilience under pressure.\n* Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with geographically distributed, crossfunctional teams.\n* Willingness and ability to travel internationally as required.Desirable\n* Experience in a customer-facing, technical support, scientific consulting, application scientist, field scientist, or business development role.\n* Experience supporting commercial opportunities, technical proposals, or customer solution development.\n* Experience presenting to external, non-academic audiences \u2014 customers, industry conferences, or webinars \u2014 rather than solely academic settings.\n* Commercial awareness and an interest in how scientific solutions translate into business opportunities.\n\n**Why Join Cyagen?**\n\n* Be part of a fast-growing global biotech company with a strong scientific reputation and AI-driven discovery platforms.\n* Work remotely, with a supportive, cross-functional international team.\n* Competitive compensation, health benefits, and opportunities for professional growth.\n* Make a real impact \u2014 your work helps researchers accelerate drug discovery and development.\n\n**Location & How to Apply**\n\nLocation: Remote \u2014 US\n\nTo apply: Send your resume to hr2@cyagen.com and tell us why you're excited about this role. We can't wait to hear from you!\n\nCyagen Biomodels LLC\n\n2255 Martin Avenue, Suite E  \nSanta Clara, CA 95050-2709, US\n\nExpected hours: 40.0 per week\n\nBenefits:\n\n* 401(k) matching\n* Dental insurance\n* Employee discount\n* Health insurance\n* Life insurance\n* Paid time off\n* Vision insurance\n\nEducation:\n\n* Doctorate (Required)\n\nExperience:\n\n* life sciences: 3 years (Required)\n\nWork Location: Remote",
